        {
          "name": "certification",
          "docs": "The claimant's Metaplex Core asset"
        }
      ],
      "checks": "Open and not expired; the claimant signed; the certification account is owned by Metaplex Core, its first byte is 1 (AssetV1), bytes 1..33 (owner) equal the claimant, byte 33 is 2 (update authority = collection) and bytes 34..66 equal the collection the bounty names. On a gated bounty (228 bytes) the program also reads the asset's plugins: PermanentFreezeDelegate must say frozen, and the Attributes plugin, written only by the update authority, must carry program and trail that hash to the trail in the terms and days_done >= min_days; no attester signs. On a 195-byte bounty an attester signs instead (the approver or ITERA_ATTESTER) and the days are its word. Records claimant and certification."
